From d2bc03f858534fd49ffc53924acedda6f13d6b79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler South <tsouth2@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 21:00:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add opt-in Windows Hello sudo guest broker

A root-only virtio port and broker let an opted-in guest approve sudo with Windows Hello. Windows answers as a WebAuthn platform authenticator: enrollment creates one ES256 credential per guest, and the broker pins its credential ID and P-256 key from the authenticator data. Each sudo request sends a fresh challenge bound to the guest, user, requesting user and TTY; Windows shows one Hello prompt and signs the client data. The broker checks the relying party hash, the user-present and user-verified flags and the signature with openssl before PAM succeeds. Anything else falls through to the guest password.

sudo try-omarchy-windows-hello enable|disable adds or removes the single PAM rule; enabling first requires the guest password. Revision 36 delivers the broker, command and port rule to existing guests without enabling anything.
